<html>
<head>
    <title>TestPlanIt</title>
    <meta name="decorator" content="atl.admin"/>
</head>
<body>
<div id="testplanit-settings-root" data-base-url="$contextPath"></div>
## Direct resource tags instead of $webResourceManager.requireResource(...):
## the SAL TemplateRenderer's velocity context does not provide
## $webResourceManager, so the require silently emitted nothing and the page
## rendered without our bundle (confirmed live: zero settings.js requests in
## the browser console). The /download/resources/ URLs are served by the
## plugin system directly and were verified live (HTTP 200). Tags sit after
## the root div so the script can mount immediately on evaluation.
<link rel="stylesheet" href="$contextPath/download/resources/io.testplanit.testplanit-jira-dc:settings-resources/settings.css">
<script src="$contextPath/download/resources/io.testplanit.testplanit-jira-dc:settings-resources/settings.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
